      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "(c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved).",
        "AbstractText": "In response to widespread recognition of the need to blend biomedical and psychosocial health care efforts, the primary care behavioral health (PCBH) model has achieved rapid uptake across the United States. Reports of its application come from military sectors, community health centers, and a variety of health care systems, large and small. Examining the PCBH model's appeal, evidence, and design forces us to confront important questions. These questions and much more are addressed in this issue of Families, Systems, & Health. (PsycINFO Database Record"
      },
